%description:
Tests TcpSocket::setNoDelay(), the socket option TCP_NODELAY. The client sends
100 bytes at t=1, 1.05 and 1.15. Nagle holds the data of t=1.05, because the
data of t=1 is not acknowledged yet. The application sets TCP_NODELAY at t=1.1:
the held data goes at once, as Linux sends the data that Nagle holds
(tcp_push_pending_frames()), and the data of t=1.15 goes at once too.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 100; 1.05 100; 1.15 100"
*.cli_app.noDelayScript="1.1 1"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[1.001 A003] A.1000 > B.2000: A 1:101(100) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.101 A004] A.1000 > B.2000: A 101:201(100) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.151 A005] A.1000 > B.2000: A 201:301(100) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.203 B002] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 301 win 16384 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
Cannot send (last) segment due to Nagle, not enough data for a full segment
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
